try_altered_copies.py: the directory <work>/rej-a lies below <work>, which another account may be able to change (its group or others can write in it, and it has no sticky bit): it could put another folder in its place and choose what runs as you. If <work> is yours, close it with chmod go-w (a further such folder below it, if any, is named in turn); otherwise name a new directory below folders that only you or root can change (such as one in your home folder, or in /tmp, whose sticky bit keeps others from replacing it); nothing was run
